---
import '../styles/global.css';
import SiteHead from '../components/SiteHead.astro';
import SiteMenu from '../components/SiteMenu.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <SiteHead ownDark />
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
  <title>Privacy Policy — LinkLasso</title>
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon-32.png" sizes="32x32" />
  <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" sizes="64x64" />
  <style is:global>
    .legal { max-width: 720px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 24px 64px; }
    .legal h1 { font-size: 30px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .legal h2 { font-size: 19px; margin-top: 32px; }
    .legal .updated { color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 24px; }
    .legal li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .legal code { background: var(--bg); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <header class="nav">
    <a class="brand" href="/"><img src="/favicon.svg" alt="" class="logo" />LinkLasso</a>
    <SiteMenu />
  </header>

  <div class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="updated">Last updated: 2026-11-24</p>

    <p>LinkLasso is a Chrome extension that lets you select multiple links on a page and open, copy or export them. This policy explains what data the extension handles.</p>

    <h2>Data stored locally</h2>
    <p>All of the following is stored in your browser via <code>chrome.storage</code> and never leaves your device except as described in "Network requests" below:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Settings</strong> — your preferences (trigger key/button, actions, filters, queue options) and saved presets.</li>
      <li><strong>Pro status</strong> — a cached flag indicating whether you have an active paid plan or trial (set by the payment provider).</li>
      <li><strong>Queue state</strong> — the list of links waiting to be opened, for the "smart queue" feature.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>Settings may sync between your Chrome profiles if you have Chrome Sync enabled (via <code>chrome.storage.sync</code>).</p>

    <h2>Network requests</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>extensionpay.com</strong> — used to check your paid/trial status and to initiate checkout. Payments are handled by <strong>Paddle</strong>, which acts as the merchant of record; LinkLasso does not see or store your card data.</li>
      <li><strong>The links you select</strong> — only when you run the "Enrich" action, LinkLasso fetches a small portion of each selected page (the first ~150 KB) to read its title, description and OpenGraph image. This happens on demand, only for the URLs you explicitly chose, and the result is placed directly into your export — it is not stored or sent anywhere else.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Sheets (optional, Pro)</strong> — only when you run the "Sheets" action, LinkLasso asks you to sign in with Google (<code>chrome.identity</code>, scope <code>https://www.googleapis.com/auth/spreadsheets</code>), creates a <strong>new</strong> spreadsheet in your own Google Drive, and writes the selected links into it (title, URL, domain, and — with enrichment — page title, description and OG image). The data travels directly from your browser to the Google Sheets API and into your account; LinkLasso does not read your existing spreadsheets or other Drive files, and does not store or send this data anywhere else. You can disconnect Google at any time from the settings.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Permissions</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>storage</strong> — for settings, cached status and queue state.</li>
      <li><strong>alarms</strong> — for the queue's resume watchdog.</li>
      <li><strong>identity</strong> — for the optional "Google Sheets" export (Google sign-in); see "Network requests".</li>
      <li><strong>bookmarks (optional)</strong> — used only when you explicitly choose "Save as bookmarks"; you can grant or revoke it at any time, and it is not required for other features.</li>
      <li><strong>Host access (&lt;all_urls&gt;)</strong> — required for the selection feature to work on every site and for the on-demand metadata fetch.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What LinkLasso does NOT do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No analytics, no tracking, no advertising.</li>
      <li>No collection or sale of personal data.</li>
      <li>No reading of your browsing history or bookmarks unless you use "Save as bookmarks".</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>ExtensionPay</strong> (extensionpay.com) — payment and Pro-status management. See their privacy policy for details.</li>
      <li><strong>Paddle</strong> — merchant of record (payments, invoicing and tax), used via ExtensionPay.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>For questions about this policy, contact the extension developer via the Chrome Web Store support link or at fodylabs.com.</p>
  </div>

  <footer class="section alt footer">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="muted">LinkLasso · Select, Open &amp; Export Multiple Links</div>
      <div class="flinks">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/terms">Terms</a>
        <a href="https://fodylabs.com">FodyLabs</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script src="/i18n.js" is:inline></script>
  <script is:inline>I18N.init();</script>
</body>
</html>
